        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Great news from "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Kent, England",
            "zh": "英国肯特郡"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "—a rare bird is back after 200 years! It’s called "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "red-billed chough",
            "zh": "红嘴山鸦"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", a clever black bird from the crow family. Long ago, these birds lived in Kent, but they disappeared because people hunted them and they lost their homes. Now, "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "wildlife",
            "ref": "v-wildlife"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " experts are helping the choughs return. They raise young birds and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "set them free",
            "ref": "v-set-free"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in nature. Recently, a young chough took its "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "first flight",
            "ref": "v-first-flight"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the wild—the first in over 200 years! It shows that the birds can find food, build nests, and even start families."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "There is a five-year plan to bring around 50 choughs to Kent. Experts are making the area safe for them. They plant wildflowers and keep insects for the birds to eat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "People in Kent are excited, too. They hope that soon the sky will be filled with these amazing birds again."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
